              <dd id="wmma-info-notes">Training-class precision. Default WMMA path on RDNA3.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>What WMMA gives you (RDNA3, gfx1100 / 1151):</h3>
      <ul class="distil-ul">
        <li>
          One dense <code>v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16</code> issue performs
          16&times;16&times;16 = <strong>4096 FMA (8192 FLOPs)</strong> over
          the tile. Throughput is a separate model: GPUOpen lists 512
          FLOPS/clk/CU fp16 dense on the 7900 XTX, i.e. &asymp; 123 TFLOPs
          theoretical at boost &mdash; a nameplate ceiling, not a measured
          hipfire number. The packed-dot2 path sits on a much lower model
          roof, qualitatively far below WMMA.
        </li>
        <li>
          Wave32 native &mdash; <code>_w32</code> suffix on the builtin.
          <code>_w64</code> WMMA builtins also exist on gfx11, but hipfire&apos;s
          primary path issues wave32.
        </li>
        <li>
          The accumulator (<code>float8_t</code> on wave32,
          <code>float16_t</code> on wave64) lives in the VGPR file, so a
          fused-GEMM kernel typically lands at <strong>80&ndash;120
          VGPRs per thread (lane)</strong> even without spills &mdash; see &sect; 06 for
          what that does to occupancy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What gfx12 WMMA (RDNA4, gfx1200+) changes:</h3>
      <ul class="distil-ul">
        <li>
          Same 16&times;16&times;16 tile, new layout: A/B pack as
          <code>half8_t</code> (8 fp16 per lane; K splits by lane group),
          the builtin becomes
          <code>__builtin_amdgcn_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16_w32_gfx12</code>,
          and the C-map moves. Most existing gfx11 kernels need their own
          <code>.gfx12.hip</code> override for the incompatible
          builtin/layout &mdash; not a wider tile. RDNA4 WMMA also adds FP8
          mixes; IU4 remains a WMMA dtype, not MFMA.
        </li>
        <li>
          gfx1100 and gfx1201 both model at 1536 VGPRs/SIMD (see &sect; 06),
          so there is no register-file growth story for the 7900 XTX class
          here &mdash; the gfx12 win is layout/throughput, not occupancy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ 4 -->
    <section class="distil-section">
      <h2><span class="num">04</span> The roofline &mdash; three matrix paths, one chip</h2>
      <p>
        Because RDNA3 ships both <code>v_wmma_*</code> and
        <code>v_dot2_f32_f16</code> (and the scalar fallback), it has
        <strong>three different compute ceilings</strong> on the same chip.
        Which one bounds you is decided by your kernel's matrix path, not by
        the GPU's nameplate TFLOPs.
      </p>

      <div class="distil-fig" data-widget="roofline">
